# The 09:10 run aborted with one reject, drivers/hid/hid-multitouch.c hunk 20
# (mt_resume/mt_remove). Upstream changed one line of that hunk's trailing
# context, in mt_remove():
#   -	timer_delete_sync(&td->release_timer);
#   +	timer_shutdown_sync(&td->release_timer);
# That is stable backport 5acb2dace582 ("HID: multitouch: stop the release
# timer from being rearmed on remove", CachyOS a0125ca86e40): a report that
# arrives after timer_delete_sync() could rearm the sticky-finger timer, which
# then fired on the freed mt_device. It is the only change to the file between
# cachyos-7.2.9-2 and cachyos-7.2.10-1.
#
# Our hunk adds the tablet-mode-switch reset and unregister_pm_notifier()
# BEFORE that line, and both still run before it, as they did before. Neither
# touches release_timer (mt_pm_notifier only drives the keyboard backlight),
# so upstream's fix and ours do not interact. The section was regenerated with
# diff -U3 -p from a real tree: the only difference from the old section is
# that context line; all 23 @@ headers are byte-identical.
#
# Checked before pushing, against a pristine cachyos-7.2.10-1 with
# dkms-clang.patch applied first, in prepare()'s order:
#   - amd-pstate-readonly-auto-sel.patch passes its -F0 gate.
#   - rebased.patch: 92 files, 0 failures, 0 rejects, 0 hunks needing fuzz,
#     32 applied at an offset; also clean as a patch -F0 dry run.
#   - surface-rtc-ec-clock.patch passes its -F0 gate after it.
#   - No duplicate MT_QUIRK_* BIT(), MT_CLS_* value or BTUSB_* BIT(); ours are
#     still BIT(27)-(29), 0x0118/0x0119 and BIT(30), and upstream took none of
#     them. No duplicate #define name in the 92 patched files that the
#     pristine tree does not also have.
