# 2026-10-21 (later the same day) -- REBASED FROM linux-surface arch-7.2.11-1.
# rebased.patch is no longer the 6.19 set carried forward; it is linux-surface's
# own patches/7.2 (15 patches, tag arch-7.2.11-1, 2026-10-18) applied to
# cachyos-7.3.0-2 and flattened. surface.config is their configs/surface-7.3.config.
# linux-surface still has no patches/7.3, so prepare() still takes the
# hand-rebase path.
#
# How: applied 0001..0015 in order to a pristine 7.3.0-2, fixed what broke,
# then regenerated every file section with diff -U3 -p against the pristine
# tree (git-style headers, real index blob ids). Same 92 files, 46 of them new,
# as the 6.19-based patch.
#
# What broke applying their 7.2 set to 7.3 (all upstream movement):
#   - 0005-ipts pci-me.c: rejected; the same table restyle as this morning.
#     Their line is identical to ours; it now uses the "{ ... }" style.
#   - 0013-cameras ipu-bridge.c: fuzz 2, the same new Lenovo/Samsung entries.
#     Lands exactly where ours did.
#   - 0013-cameras ov8865.c: both commits ("Drop the runtime PM usage count on
#     stream failure", "Program the sensor on stream start") are upstream in
#     7.3 as 3fe797a12bfa and 4e1446ac169a; 7.3's ov8865_s_stream() and
#     ov8865_resume() match the patched result line for line. Dropped.
#   - 0015-hid-surface drivers/hid/Makefile: fuzz 1, landed correctly.
#
# What this changes against this morning's 6.19-based patch, found by applying
# both to 7.3.0-2 and diffing the resulting files (only 5 files differ):
#   - drivers/hid/ipts/desc.h: IPTS_HID_REPORT_DATA_SIZE 7485 -> 7488, their
#     5eb5954034da "hid: ipts: Fix size of synthesized HID data report"
#     (linux-surface #2150, PR #2233). Since hid-core 0a3fe972a7cb, which IS in
#     7.3.0-2, a report shorter than its descriptor is dropped, which broke IPTS
#     touch on fallback-descriptor devices (e.g. Surface Book 1). A real fix the
#     6.19 set lacked.
#   - int3472/discrete.c: their version fixes the two -Wformat warnings every
#     7.2 build printed (%lx for gpio_flags, a "0x02x" missing its %). Same
#     logic otherwise.
#   - hid-multitouch.c: they fixed upstream's BIT(26)/0x0117 collision
#     themselves, with the same free values in a different order:
#     TYPE_COVER_BACKLIGHT BIT(27), TABLET_MODE_SWITCH BIT(28),
#     SKIP_MODESET_ON_HW_OPEN_CLOSE BIT(29); TYPE_COVER 0x0118, TOUCHPAD
#     0x0119. The touchpad class/device entries moved after the type cover's.
#     Lookups are by class name and product ID, so order does not matter.
#   - iommu.c (same IPTS quirk, placed elsewhere) and drivers/hid/Makefile
#     (ipts/ithc line placement): cosmetic.
#   - btusb.c: they also chose BIT(30) for BTUSB_LOWER_LESCAN_INTERVAL;
